# =============================================================================
# colopaint3D_paper
#
# NOTE ON ORDERING: the upstream repo excluded *.csv / *.pdf / *.png outright,
# which silently swallowed the per-panel source-data tables. Here the excludes
# are narrow and the source_data/ allow-rules are explicit. If you add a new
# ignore rule, check `git status` still shows source_data/*.csv afterwards.
# =============================================================================

# --- Downloaded / generated, never committed --------------------------------
/data/
# NOTE: this must exclude figures/ *contents*, not the directory. git does not descend
# into an excluded directory, so with a bare `/figures/` the negations below never fire
# and the archived originals were silently absent from every clone.
/figures/*
# ...except the archived January-2026 originals, which cannot be regenerated
!/figures/archived_originals/
!/figures/archived_originals/**
# Intermediate tables a notebook writes next to itself (e.g. exp1 QCFlags.csv).
# The committed inputs live in analysis/**/data/, which is allow-listed below.
analysis/**/results/

# --- Large binary data formats ---------------------------------------------
*.parquet
*.h5ad
*.tif
*.tiff
*.npy

# --- Environments and caches ----------------------------------------------
.venv/
.venv*/
venv*/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store

# --- Notebook execution artefacts ------------------------------------------
# papermill writes an executed copy next to each notebook
*.executed.ipynb

# =============================================================================
# EXPLICITLY TRACKED — these must survive every rule above
# =============================================================================

# Per-panel source data: the point of this repo. Committed.
!/source_data/
!/source_data/**/*.csv
!/source_data/MANIFEST.csv

# Small analysis inputs shipped with the notebooks (sphere detection, cached tables)
!/analysis/**/data/
!/analysis/**/data/**

# Acquisition protocols: instrument config, not data. Small, and the one part
# of the method a reader cannot reconstruct from the notebooks.
!/acquisition/
!/acquisition/**

# Scratch comparison renders — working notes, not part of the release
/checks/

# Upload bundles built from data/ — regenerable, never committed
*.zip
